# PatternForge / ApexCaliber Rules (`.clinerules`)

> **Canonical Rules:** This repository is governed by [AGENTS.md](./AGENTS.md), [DESIGN.md](./DESIGN.md), [UX-CONTRACT.md](./UX-CONTRACT.md), and modular workspace rules under [`.agents/rules/`](./.agents/rules/). Keep this file aligned as a quick compatibility pointer.

1. **Cobalt Studio & Zero Slop:** Follow `.agents/rules/01-design-invariants.md` and `02-geometry-and-type.md` (Cobalt palette `#101522` / `#182132` dark & `#F3F5F9` / `#FFFFFF` light; zero violet/lavender; concentric corner math $R_{inner} = R_{outer} - P$; max 2 container levels; zero single-sided card borders).
2. **Dark Night Zone Contrast:** Code editors, stages, and canvases must carry `data-zone="night"` or `.stage` and consume semantic surface tokens (`var(--surface-*)`, `text-chalk`, `text-muted`).
3. **Motion & Interactive Completeness:** Follow `.agents/rules/03-motion-and-visualizers.md` and `04-interactive-states.md` (GPU `transform`/`opacity` only, approved easing, `>=44px` mobile hit targets, visible focus rings on sliders/controls, shape-matched skeletons, `prefers-reduced-motion`).
4. **3-Step Question Pedagogical Flow (`/q/:slug`) & Zero Empty-Textarea Busywork:**
   - Step 1 (`1. Learn DS & Pattern`): Teach underlying Data Structure, idioms, and complexity math before coding, presenting structured Study Exemplars first.
   - Step 2 (`2. Code in Terminal`): Fullscreen draggable split-pane IDE preserving native `<select>` ownership.
   - Step 3 (`3. Interview Answer Guide`): Full-width structured interview walkthrough.
